= Solution
{parent=1}

Use integral <cellular homology>. All three vertices become a single vertex, and all three oriented edges become one oriented <circle>, with generator $a$. The face goes round that circle three times in the same direction. Thus the quotient has a <CW complex> structure with one cell in each of dimensions zero, one and two, and <cellular chain complex>
$$
0\longrightarrow\mathbb Z\xrightarrow{\;3\;}\mathbb Z\xrightarrow{\;0\;}\mathbb Z\longrightarrow0.
$$
The degree-two boundary is injective and its cokernel is $\mathbb Z/3$. Therefore
$$
\boxed{H_j(X;\mathbb Z)=\begin{cases}\mathbb Z,&j=0,\\\mathbb Z/3,&j=1,\\0,&j\geq2.\end{cases}}
$$
The attaching word is $a^3$, so the <Seifert-van Kampen theorem> also gives $\pi_1(X)\cong\mathbb Z/3$. This is the degree-three circle-attachment model of a <Moore space>.

